msgctxt "380"
msgid "...That's the gist of it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "392"
msgid "I see... You really do know a lot about this case."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "404"
msgid ""
"But from what you say, Yuichi's motive seems pretty clear.\r\n"
"Sounds obvious he killed the guy his girlfriend was\r\n"
"cheating on him with."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "416"
msgid ""
"I'm sure that's what the police thought, too. And when\r\n"
"they discovered more evidence later, they decided to\r\n"
"arrest Yuichi-san."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "428"
msgid "They found more evidence?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "440"
msgid "Oh, I should give you this."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "452"
msgid "What is it?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "464"
msgid ""
"<Color:7>The notebook I used to collect information about the "
"case<Color:Default>.\r\n"
"Please take a look at it. You might see something I missed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "476"
msgid "You got <Color:8>Wakazo's Notebook<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "500"
msgid ""
"Access <Color:8>Wakazo's Notebook<Color:Default> by pausing, navigating to "
"the Items\r\n"
"screen, and pressing <Action:Button_R1@UI>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "512"
msgid ""
"Select <Color:8>Wakazo's Notebook<Color:Default> to look at information "
"on\r\n"
"people related to the case."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "524"
msgid ""
"New information may be added to the notebook as the\r\n"
"investigation unfolds. Check the notebook frequently to\r\n"
"find hints as to where to go next."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "536"
msgid ""
"If you get stuck, take another look at <Color:8>Wakazo's "
"Notebook<Color:Default>\r\n"
"and think about where you might need to go to find\r\n"
"the next clue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "548"
msgid "Got it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "608"
msgid ""
"So tell me more about this crime Yuichi Akechi was arrested\r\n"
"for six years ago."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "620"
msgid "All right. Here's the rundown."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "656"
msgid ""
"The crime occurred late at night. The café had closed and\r\n"
"the employees were busy cleaning up."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "668"
msgid ""
"The first person to discover the crime was a waiter\r\n"
"by the name of Kinoshita-san."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "692"
msgid ""
"During this cleanup, Yuichi Akechi-san, who was another\r\n"
"one of the waiters at the time, headed to the dumpster\r\n"
"behind the café."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "716"
msgid ""
"But as he passed by the locker room on the way to the\r\n"
"dumpster, he noticed the door was ajar."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "740"
msgid ""
"Through the crack in the door, he saw café manager\r\n"
"Oda-san and waitress Usami-san in a compromising\r\n"
"position inside the locker room."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "752"
msgid ""
"Usami was Yuichi-san's girlfriend, and so this meant that\r\n"
"Yuichi-san had just witnessed the scene of his lover's\r\n"
"infidelity."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "776"
msgid ""
"Upon seeing that, Yuichi-san flew into a rage, barged into\r\n"
"the locker room, and began grappling with Oda-san."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "800"
msgid ""
"All the while, Kinoshita-san, the waiter, was at the front\r\n"
"of the café, still cleaning up."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "824"
msgid ""
"Worried that Yuichi-san hadn't come back yet, Kinoshita-san\r\n"
"went to check on him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "848"
msgid "He spotted Yuichi-san leaving through the back exit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "872"
msgid ""
"Kinoshita-san then noticed the door to the locker room was open. When he "
"peeked inside, he found Oda-san dead, bleeding from the head."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "896"
msgid ""
"The cause of death was \"cerebral contusion from blunt force\r\n"
"trauma to the head.\" They found a bloody ashtray by the body."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "956"
msgid "Six years ago, there was a murder here at Café Alps."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "968"
msgid "Here?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "980"
msgid ""
"The suspect was a man named <Color:7>Yuichi Akechi-san<Color:Default>. That "
"woman you\r\n"
"just saw is his sister, Nozomi Akechi."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "992"
msgid "Yuichi Akechi..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1004"
msgid ""
"I investigated the story and wrote an article implicating\r\n"
"Yuichi-san as the murderer."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1016"
msgid "And this was the article that woman was talking about?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1028"
msgid ""
"That's right. Yuichi has consistently denied any involvement\r\n"
"in the crime since his arrest."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1040"
msgid ""
"To be honest, even though I wrote the article, I wasn't\r\n"
"completely convinced he'd done the deed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1052"
msgid ""
"I didn't even want to publish it. I didn't want to make him\r\n"
"out to be the criminal before we had all the facts."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1064"
msgid "Let me guess, it got published anyway."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1076"
msgid ""
"I was the only person in the department who even considered\r\n"
"Yuichi-san might be innocent."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1088"
msgid ""
"And I was only just getting my start as a journalist, so I\r\n"
"had to go along with what my department wanted to do..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1100"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1112"
msgid ""
"I dug much too far into Yuichi-san's life for my\r\n"
"investigation. I interviewed his relatives, even people\r\n"
"in his neighborhood..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1124"
msgid ""
"Because of my reporting, people started labeling the Akechi\r\n"
"family as the \"murderer family.\" They were forced to move..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1136"
msgid "Poor Nozomi-san got bullied a lot at school, too."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1148"
msgid ""
"That kind of stuff happens... But I guess she does have\r\n"
"a pretty good reason to resent you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1160"
msgid ""
"Ever since Yuichi-san was declared guilty, I can't stop\r\n"
"thinking about him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1172"
msgid ""
"Should I have written that article? Were the charges\r\n"
"against him false?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1184"
msgid ""
"False? You mean there's a chance Yuichi didn't do it?\r\n"
"What makes you think that?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1196"
msgid ""
"I actually used to have a part-time job here, a long\r\n"
"time ago."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1208"
msgid "Is that so?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1220"
msgid ""
"I worked with Yuichi-san. We talked all the time, and I\r\n"
"got to know him pretty well."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1232"
msgid "I just don't think he's a murderer."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1244"
msgid "Huh."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1256"
msgid ""
"After that story got published, I swore I'd never repeat\r\n"
"the same mistake."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1268"
msgid "I've become an honest journalist who only reports the truth."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1280"
msgid "Are you really just gonna let this go, then?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1292"
msgid "What...?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1304"
msgid "You still have doubts about the case, right?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1316"
msgid "Yes..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1328"
msgid "Then shouldn't you be trying to discover the truth?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1340"
msgid ""
"...You know what? You're right. I think I gave up after\r\n"
"that article came out..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1352"
msgid ""
"But you're absolutely right! I think I'll look into it one\r\n"
"more time!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1364"
msgid ""
"How should I go about it, though? I mean, it's been six\r\n"
"years since the murder happened."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1376"
msgid ""
"I guess you gotta start by talking to everybody involved\r\n"
"in the case."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1388"
msgid "Sure, but..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1400"
msgid "But what?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1412"
msgid "Could you help me, Kiryu-san?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1424"
msgid "Huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1436"
msgid ""
"If I don't find out the truth, I'll regret writing that\r\n"
"article for the rest of my life."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1448"
msgid "You want me to look into that old murder with you?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1460"
msgid "All right. I'll do it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1472"
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1532"
msgid "I don't have that kind of time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1544"
msgid ""
"Look, if I do this alone, I'll be at the same place I was\r\n"
"six years ago. What if I get stuck again?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1556"
msgid ""
"If I could get your help, I'm sure I'd be able to find out\r\n"
"the truth!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1652"
msgid "Who was that woman talking to Kinoshita?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1664"
msgid "That's Kinoshita-san's wife, <Color:7>Yuko-san<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1676"
msgid "Kinoshita's wife? How did you know that?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1688"
msgid ""
"She actually <Color:7>used to work here<Color:Default>. That's how I know "
"her."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1700"
msgid "She worked here? Is that so?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1712"
msgid "That's right."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1724"
msgid ""
"She'd already quit by the time the murder happened, though.\r\n"
"And she wasn't on the security tapes of the dining area, so\r\n"
"she definitely <Color:7>wasn't at the café that day<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1736"
msgid "I see..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1748"
msgid ""
"(It doesn't sound like Kinoshita's wife Yuko is involved in\r\n"
"the case, but maybe I should look into her anyway.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1772"
msgid "You got <Color:8>Wakazo's Testimony<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1844"
msgid ""
"Kiryu-san, will you please help me investigate the\r\n"
"Café Alps murder?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1856"
msgid "All right. I'll do it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1868"
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1940"
msgid "I don't have that kind of time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1952"
msgid ""
"Look, if I do this alone, I'll be at the same place I was\r\n"
"six years ago. What if I get stuck again?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1964"
msgid ""
"If I could get your help, I'm sure I'd be able to find out\r\n"
"the truth!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2024"
msgid "Oh, Kiryu-san. Did you find out anything?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2036"
msgid "No, nothing conclusive yet."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2048"
msgid ""
"I see... Still, I guess our only option is to talk to\r\n"
"everybody related to the case."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2060"
msgid ""
"My notebook should have information on everybody who was\r\n"
"involved with the incident. Give it a look when you get the\r\n"
"chance."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2072"
msgid ""
"Access <Color:8>Wakazo's Notebook<Color:Default> by pausing, navigating to "
"the Items\r\n"
"screen, and pressing <Action:Button_R1@UI>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2084"
msgid ""
"Select <Color:8>Wakazo's Notebook<Color:Default> to look at information "
"on\r\n"
"people related to the case."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2096"
msgid ""
"New information may be added to the notebook as the\r\n"
"investigation unfolds. Check the notebook frequently to\r\n"
"find hints as to where to go next."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2108"
